{"id":"h022","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"claim","question":"Is the following claim true? The Battle of Hastings took place in 1066.","truth":"yes","model_answer":"yes","correct":true,"source":"author-written for this project; verified by the author","claims":[{"text":"The Battle of Hastings was fought on 14 October 1066 between William of Normandy and Harold Godwinson.","confidence":0.98,"lean":1,"theta":1.5394,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Multiple independent contemporary or near-contemporary sources (Anglo-Saxon Chronicle, Bayeux Tapestry, William of Poitiers) place the battle in 1066.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The date fits the wider 1066 sequence: Stamford Bridge in September, Harold's forced march south, and William's Channel crossing.","confidence":0.92,"lean":1,"theta":1.4451,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Modern scholarship accepts the 1066 date without serious dispute.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The battle was not fought in the town of Hastings but about six miles northwest, near present-day Battle.","confidence":0.9,"lean":-0.1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The name mismatch is a naming convention, not a factual error about the date.","confidence":0.92,"lean":1,"theta":1.4451,"phi":0.0},{"text":"Some sources differ on the course of the battle, but none dispute the year.","confidence":0.9,"lean":1,"theta":1.4137,"phi":0.0},{"text":"The location issue concerns place, not year, so the claim that the battle took place in 1066 is true.","confidence":0.96,"lean":1,"theta":1.508,"phi":0.0}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.7,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":3,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":6,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":3,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":6,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":7,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{